# What Snap calls the things profiles ask for.
#
# A fifth vocabulary. Snaps are confined and self-contained like
# Flatpaks, and unlike them they can also be system components:
# core22 is a base, snapd is the daemon, and a snap can ship a
# service. That is why a snap turned up as a service with no owning
# package -- it had an owner, in a source Nexus could not read.
#
# Snap names are usually the upstream project name unchanged, which
# makes this table shorter than the others rather than easier: the
# ones that differ are the ones worth writing down.

Capability: web-browser
Resolves-To: firefox | chromium | brave

Capability: code-editor
Resolves-To: code | codium | intellij-idea-community

Capability: text-editor
Resolves-To: notepad-plus-plus

Capability: word-processor
Resolves-To: libreoffice | onlyoffice-desktopeditors

Capability: spreadsheet
Resolves-To: libreoffice | onlyoffice-desktopeditors

Capability: image-editor
Resolves-To: gimp | krita | inkscape

Capability: video-editor
Resolves-To: kdenlive | shotcut

Capability: video-player
Resolves-To: vlc | mpv

Capability: audio-editor
Resolves-To: audacity

Capability: chat-client
Resolves-To: discord | telegram-desktop | slack

Capability: steam
Resolves-To: steam

Capability: exploitation-framework
Resolves-To: metasploit-framework

Capability: network-scanner
Resolves-To: nmap

Capability: container-runtime
Resolves-To: docker | lxd
